+<div class="cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class="prompt input_prompt">
+</div><div class="inner_cell">
+<div class="text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
+<h2 id="Run-Harmony">Run Harmony<a class="anchor-link" href="#Run-Harmony">&#182;</a></h2><p>The simplest way to run Harmony is to pass the Seurat object and specify which variable(s) to integrate out. RunHarmony returns a Seurat object, updated with the corrected Harmony coordinates. Let's set plot_convergence to TRUE, so we can make sure that the Harmony objective function gets better with each round.</p>
+
+</div>
+</div>
+</div>
+<div class="cell border-box-sizing code_cell rendered">
+<div class="input">
+<div class="prompt input_prompt">In&nbsp;[100]:</div>
+<div class="inner_cell">
+    <div class="input_area">
+<div class=" highlight hl-r"><pre><span></span><span class="nf">options</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">repr.plot.height</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="m">2.5</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">repr.plot.width</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="m">6</span><span class="p">)</span>
+<span class="n">pbmc</span> <span class="o">&lt;-</span> <span class="n">pbmc</span> <span class="o">%&gt;%</span> 
+    <span class="nf">RunHarmony</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">&quot;stim&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">plot_convergence</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="kc">TRUE</span><span class="p">)</span>
+</pre></div>
+
+    </div>
+</div>
+</div>
+
+<div class="output_wrapper">
+<div class="output">
+
+
+<div class="output_area">
+
+    <div class="prompt"></div>
+
+
+<div class="output_subarea output_stream output_stderr output_text">
+<pre>Harmony 1/10
+Harmony 2/10
